## 2. Core new construction to investigate

Use F2={0,1}, with XOR as field addition and AND as field multiplication.

Let V=F2^4 with ordered basis e0,e1,e2,e3 corresponding to the four cells / atomic truth positions of a binary CM in a fixed cyclic ordering.

Define the order-four cyclic rotation operator

    R e_j = e_(j+1 mod 4)

so R^4=I and R^T=R^-1.

For a=(a0,a1,a2,a3) in F2^4, define

    Lambda(a) = a0 I XOR a1 R XOR a2 R^2 XOR a3 R^3.

Define

    N = I XOR R.

This is the central construction.

A major conceptual question is whether a nontrivial phase/interference/modal operator theory can be **derived from the geometric rotation symmetry of an independently motivated Boolean logical-operator representation**, rather than postulated as a finite-field quantum state theory at the outset.

