## 21. Final synthesis question

At the end answer:

> After all known mathematics and prior art are stripped away, what is the genuinely distinctive research object?

A candidate thesis to test, not assume, is:

> A Boolean logical-operator representation has a native four-position geometric rotation. Lifting that rotation generates a restricted rotation-equivariant algebra. The logical semantics of the original truth-function representation then induce nontrivial correspondences between Boolean properties and operator properties, and the resulting restricted algebra supports a finite modal measurement theory whose contextuality/resource structure differs from the unrestricted finite-field theory.

Determine whether that thesis survives rigorous scrutiny. If so, formulate the strongest defensible version. If not, identify the narrower thesis that does.

Optimize for correctness, priority accuracy, and a publishable mathematical result rather than for flattering conclusions.
